# Connections Control File for the zrouter GUI POC (real nets from board.brd).
#
# Grammar (doc/zcoms/zchap.html, "The Connections Control File"):
#   <I/O refdes> <net> <extend_layer> <min#vias> [<max#vias>]
#   * <net> <shape_layer> <extend_layer> <percentage_shape_coverage>
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored; lines are routed in file order. Fields are
# separated by one or more spaces/tabs and must stay in this order.
#
# The board (runs/artwork_test/board.brd) has 2 layers: TOP and BOTTOM, 81 ICs,
# 0 existing vias, and a real GND net carrying pins U1.12, U1.8, etc. We ask zrouter to
# extend a via from U1's GND pin(s) down to the BOTTOM ETCH subclass (1 via each), which
# is exactly the "connect GND pins of a module to the ground plane" use case.
#
# NOTE: zrouter only acts on I/O pins of *MLC modules*; U1/U8 are here ordinary ICs. If
# zrouter finds no MLC module it will route nothing and write no Zrouter.log — that is a
# valid outcome of this test, not a hang. See the POC report for the full assessment.
U1 GND BOTTOM 1
U8 GND BOTTOM 1
U1 * BOTTOM 1 1
